# Act 3, chapter 9 "Years of Terror" (Age 768-774). Flags: 360 opened, 361 Bulma, 362 bunker arrival, 363 Super 13
# destroyed, 364 Gohan fought, 365 after Super 13 seen, 366 chapter end, 367 Android 13 awake, 438 Android 13 beaten
# (phase 1, row 11), 439 transformation seen (phase 2 = Super 13) (each scene sets its flag and reloads the incubator:
# enemy conditions are only read at load). Areas (world 17, act3 palette): 17:11 Capsule
# Corporation, 17:12-17:15 Gero's Act 1 bunker (Super 13 = stats row 21, actor super13), 17:16/17:17 West City (Gohan,
# BF's own Gohan sprite, row 22). Speakers: #17 Bulma, #209/#210/#211 Androids 13/14/15 (Prototype D portraits),
# future_gohan_twoarm.N (R4b).
list ch9_start
set_flag 360
do call 149 1
do call 183 516 1466 1467
do call 115 0 2 0 0 0; call 121 1
do call 120 1; call 119 17 11 1 240 330; call 121 60
narrate Age 768. A year after West City, half the world's cities are rubble.
narrate Nobody fights back any more. People just run, and hide, and listen to the radio for the two numbers.
say android17 Capsule Corporation. Richest family on the planet. Let's see what rich people keep.
say android18 It's empty. They're all gone.
say android17 Not all of them. Somebody left a light on.
journal Search Capsule Corporation
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- Bulma (by the dome house)
list ch9_bulma
if_flag 361 bulma_again
set_flag 361
narrate A woman stands in front of the dome house. She is holding a baby wrapped in a lab coat, and she does not move.
say #17 Stay back. If you're going to do it, just do it. But leave him out of it. He's a baby.
say android17 Relax, lady. You're not worth the energy.
narrate The baby grabs at the air and laughs at nothing. Eighteen can't look away from him.
narrate A woman's voice, singing off key. A small boy asleep with his head in her lap. The song is clear. Her face is not.
say android18 ...What's his name?
say #17 Trunks.
say android18 Weird name.
say #17 His father thought so too.
say android17 His father. Let me guess. Spiky hair, bad attitude, wanted a rematch with a dead man?
narrate The woman doesn't answer. She holds the baby tighter, and her eyes don't leave Seventeen's face.
say android18 Come on, Seventeen. There's nothing here.
narrate Every screen in the building flickers on at once. The radio on the porch crackles.
narrate Voice: Units Seventeen and Eighteen. Return to base. Repeat: Units Seventeen and Eighteen, return to base.
say android17 Gero's leftovers. That old computer is still running.
say android18 Then let's go and switch it off.
narrate They leave without looking back. The woman stands in the doorway for a long time after they're gone.
do call 120 60
do call 119 17 37 1 24 296; call 121 60
stop
label bulma_again
say #17 ...Go. Please. Just go.
# ---------- the bunker (17:12 arrival)
list ch9_bunker
if_flag 362 bunker_seen
set_flag 362
narrate Gero's old bunker in the northern mountains. Twenty years of dust, and the power is on.
narrate Computer: Welcome home, Units Seventeen and Eighteen.
say android18 He built this place before he built us. I can feel it in the walls.
narrate Computer: Construction log. Unit Fourteen: parts harvested.
say #210 ...
narrate Computer: Unit Fifteen: parts harvested.
say #211 ...
narrate Computer: Unit Thirteen: complete. Primary directive: destroy Son Goku. Target deceased. Secondary directive: recover or destroy the defective units.
say android17 Defective? We're the best thing he ever made.
narrate Computer: Unit Thirteen is waiting for you in the incubator.
journal Find Unit Thirteen
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label bunker_seen
list ch9_pod16
narrate An empty pod. Scratched into the label: 16. DO NOT ACTIVATE.
say android18 Whatever was in here, he was scared of it.
say android17 Or it was too nice to keep. Same thing, to him.
# ---------- Super 13 (17:14 arrival, fight)
list ch9_thirteen
set_flag 367
do heal
narrate The incubator hisses open. A man steps out: white hair, a trucker's cap, hands in his pockets like he's waiting for a bus.
say #209 Units Seventeen. Eighteen. Your creator ordered your return. You refused.
say #209 I was built to obey him. It is the only thing I will ever do.
say android17 Gero's dead, pal. Nobody's giving orders any more.
say #209 Then I will obey a dead man.
say android18 ...That's what we'd be. If we'd listened.
do call 120 20; call 119 17 14 1 208 312; call 121 20
journal Destroy Android 13
do call 47; call 51 0
# ---------- phase 2 (17:14 arrival after Android 13 is beaten, flag 438): he absorbs 14 and 15
list ch9_thirteen2
set_flag 439
do heal
narrate Thirteen goes down hard. Then the floor starts to hum.
narrate Computer: Unit Thirteen, critical damage. Contingency. Integrating Units Fourteen and Fifteen.
# (2026-11-03) the absorption on screen: the 17:50 backdrop (this room's map, Android 13 playing the user's 6-frame
# absorption as his idle), loaded with native 115 (camera top-left 112,196: him above the text box); 119 below returns
do call 120 20; call 115 17 50 1 112 196; call 121 20
say #209 ...Yes.
narrate Two capsules open in the wall. What's left of Fourteen and Fifteen flies to him, and he grows around it.
# (2026-11-03, user: "a white flash like the fusion dance") natives 122 / 123 = fade to white / back from white (BF's
# fusion-style flash; likely, they mirror 120 / 121 with the white fade classes 0x0804BBD4 / 0x0804C5B8): two quick
# strobes, hold white, reload with Super 13 there, come back out of the white
do call 122 6; call 123 6; call 122 6; call 123 6; call 122 24
do call 119 17 14 1 208 312; call 123 40
narrate Blue skin. A red mane. The parts of two other androids, grown into one.
say #209 Now I am complete.
say android17 Great. Now he's bigger.
journal Destroy Super 13
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch9_after13
if_flag 365 after13_seen
set_flag 365
narrate Super 13 doesn't fall so much as come apart. Fourteen's arm. Fifteen's hat. Thirteen's face, still calm.
narrate Computer: Unit Thirteen... offline. Directive... directive...
narrate Seventeen puts a fist through the console. The lights go out for the last time.
say android18 He obeyed right up to the end. That's the saddest thing I've ever seen.
say android17 You're getting weird, Eighteen.
say android18 Maybe.
narrate Years pass.
do call 120 60
do call 119 17 18 1 240 150; call 121 60
stop
label after13_seen
# ---------- the hub years (Age 772): Capsule Corporation is the twins' base. Optional: Mt. Paozu (airship), Roshi's
# island (hangar). The gate leads on to Gohan. Flags 368 hub opened, 370 Chi-Chi, 371 Roshi.
list ch9_hub
if_flag 368 hub_seen
set_flag 368
narrate Age 772. The twins have taken Capsule Corporation for themselves. Nobody comes to take it back.
say android18 Her things are still here. Baby clothes in a box. A photo of a man with spiky hair, scowling at the camera.
say android17 Don't get sentimental. It's just a house with a lot of toys in it.
journal Fly anywhere you like: the airship pad or the hangar. West City's crossroads when you're ready.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label hub_seen
list ch9_hub18
if_flag 440 h18_dressed
set_flag 440
say android18 I went through her closets. She had good taste. For a human.
say android17 You're wearing her clothes?
say android18 We're wearing her clothes. Here. Something that isn't Red Ribbon issue.
narrate (New outfits for both of you. Select Outfit with the L Button: each press of the B Button changes into the next one.)
stop
label h18_dressed
if_flag 370 h18_paozu
if_flag 371 h18_roshi
say android18 Go wherever you want. I'll catch up.
stop
label h18_paozu
if_flag 371 h18_both
say android18 That woman on the mountain. She looked at me like she felt sorry for me. Nobody's allowed to feel sorry for me.
stop
label h18_roshi
say android18 The old man knew his name. Krillin. I didn't want to know his name.
stop
label h18_both
say android18 Every one of them had somebody waiting at home. Do you think anybody ever waited for us?
say android17 If they did, they stopped.
list ch9_fly_paozu
if_flag 370 paozu_done
narrate Seventeen gets Bulma's old airship started on the third try.
do call 120 40; call 119 17 19 1 112 120; call 121 40
stop
label paozu_done
say android17 We've been to the mountain. Nothing there but a grave and a stubborn woman.
list ch9_fly_kame
if_flag 371 kame_done
narrate The hangar is full of jets nobody will ever fly again. Seventeen takes the fastest one.
do call 120 40; call 119 17 20 1 380 300; call 121 40
stop
label kame_done
say android17 Nothing out there but an old man and a lot of water.
# Mt. Paozu, Goku's house (17:19 arrival)
list ch9_paozu
if_flag 370 paozu_seen
set_flag 370
narrate Mount Paozu. A small round house in the trees, and a grave out front with fresh flowers on it.
narrate Inside, a woman is setting the table for two.
say #20 If you're looking for Gohan, he isn't here. He hasn't been home in four months. He's out there looking for you.
say android17 Then you should have kept him home.
say #20 I tried. I lost his father to a sickness and I'm losing him to the two of you.
say #20 Every night I set his plate out anyway.
say android18 Why? He might not come back.
say #20 Because if he does, he'll be hungry.
say #20 Do you have a mother, girl?
say android18 ...I don't remember.
say #20 Then somebody, somewhere, set a plate out for you once. And waited.
narrate Hands that smell of soap, pushing hair out of a little girl's eyes. Eighteen's own hands are shaking.
say android17 Let's go. This place is depressing.
narrate Eighteen looks at the empty plate for a long time.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label paozu_seen
# Roshi's island (17:20 arrival)
list ch9_kame
if_flag 371 kame_seen
set_flag 371
narrate A small island in the middle of the ocean. Kame House is a pile of pink boards.
narrate An old man sits on the sand in front of it, watching the water.
say #74 Took you long enough. I've buried every one of my students. Go on, then.
say android17 Who were they?
say #74 Goku. Krillin. Yamcha, more or less. Tien, when he'd let me. Good boys, every one of them.
say android18 Krillin. The short one.
say #74 That's him. Always wanted a normal life, you know. A little house. A wife. Somebody to come home to. Never got around to it.
say android18 ...He held back. When we fought. He wouldn't hit me.
say #74 That sounds like him. He could always see something in people the rest of us missed.
narrate Eighteen doesn't say anything for a long time.
say android17 You're not even going to beg?
say #74 I'm three hundred years old, sonny. I'm done begging.
say android17 ...Boring.
narrate They turn their backs on him. He doesn't watch them go.
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label kame_seen
# the gate -> Gohan (Age 774)
list ch9_to_gohan
narrate Age 774. Seven years after West City.
do call 120 60; call 119 17 16 1 424 440; call 121 60
# ---------- Gohan (17:16 arrival, fight)
list ch9_gohan
narrate The ruins of West City. Someone has been waiting in the middle of the crossroads.
say future_gohan_twoarm.0 Seven years. I've trained for seven years for this.
say android17 Hey, it's Piccolo's kid. You got tall.
say future_gohan_twoarm.2 Don't you dare say his name.
say android18 You should have stayed hidden. You'd have lived longer.
say future_gohan_twoarm.1 Maybe. But somebody has to stand up to you.
journal Fight Gohan
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch9_end
if_flag 366 end9_seen
set_flag 366
narrate Gohan crashes through what's left of a wall. When the dust settles, he is gone.
narrate On the street: a torn sleeve, and a lot of blood.
say android18 He'll come back.
say android17 Good. He's the only one left who's any fun.
say android18 ...He lost his arm, Lapis.
say android17 Don't call me that.
narrate Eighteen looks at the blood on the road for a long time. Then she follows her brother.
journal Seven years
narrate End of Chapter 9.
run ch10_start
stop
label end9_seen
# ---------- the way to the bunker (areas from log4/gen_ch9.py; flags 400 pass, 401 Sentinel, 402 mine cache)
list ch9_pass
set_flag 400
narrate The northern mountains. The bunker door is set into the cliff to the west, and it is shut.
narrate Computer: Units Seventeen and Eighteen. Before you may enter: evaluation. The creator would have wanted it.
narrate Computer: Power to the bunker door has been routed through the generator cave. A Sentinel guards it. Prove your worth.
say android18 Even dead, he's still testing us.
say android17 Fine. Let's break his toys. East, then. The cave.
journal Destroy the {c07}Sentinel{c02} in the generator cave
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch9_sealed
narrate The bunker door. Solid steel, and no power to it. Somewhere east, a generator hums behind something big.
list ch9_cache_mine
if_flag 402 c9mine_empty
set_flag 402
narrate The old mining cart. Under the junk, a crate the drone never found: two Hercule-ades and a Senzu Bean.
do call 129 6 2; call 129 11 1
stop
label c9mine_empty
narrate Nothing but rocks.
# ---------- Gero's notes 7-9 (log4/gen_more.py: bunker 17:12, generator cave 17:38, old mine 17:39; flags 526-528)
list note_bunker
if_flag 526 nbunk_read
set_flag 526
narrate Tucked behind the old tank's gauge: a child's drawing, folded into a notebook page. A stick figure and a robot, holding hands.
narrate Under it, in Gero's handwriting: "Gevo, age six: Papa, can robots be sad? I told him no."
say android18 Who's Gevo?
say android17 Some kid. Before us.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nbunk_read
narrate The old tank. Nothing else tucked behind it.
list note_cave
if_flag 527 ncave_read
set_flag 527
narrate A notebook page jammed behind the generator's housing.
narrate "Unit 16 shelved. He has my son's face, and he will not hurt anything that lives. I could not bring myself to scrap him."
say android18 Sixteen. The big one in the pod.
say android17 He kept that one. Interesting.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label ncave_read
narrate The generator hums. Nothing else is hidden here.
list note_mine
if_flag 528 nmine_read
set_flag 528
narrate Under a rock by the cave wall: a notebook page, soaked and dried a dozen times.
narrate "The computer will finish Project Cell long after I am gone. A perfect creature with no will but mine."
narrate "I should be glad. I find I would rather have had two children who never listened."
say android18 ...
say android17 He means us, doesn't he.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nmine_read
narrate Rocks and old timbers.
